description:
muse (read_only: hard, reads_files: true) can take file-list briefs, but leaves no read trace, so only its own files_examined list and the citation check apply. muse is early in the low-medium and medium-high chains. The decision record leaves open whether a muse SHIP on a file-list brief needs a second reviewer.

Options:
- require a traced second reviewer for a muse SHIP on a file-list brief;
- add a muse read trace;
- accept the risk with a documented reason;
- cheap option: set muse `reads_files: false` in .github/oracle-reviewers.yml until muse leaves a read trace. Then muse only takes inline briefs. Cost: more pending results when codex is out of quota, because muse can no longer be the reviewer for file-list briefs. See oracle-muse-invalid-verdict-output-20261009 for muse's other reliability problem.

agy is covered by oracle-agy-reviewer-calibration-20261008.
